# Driven by the systemd user unit swayidle.service (`swayidle -w`).
#
# Noctalia is the locker. Every lock trigger funnels through logind's
# session-lock signal (`loginctl lock-session`), which Noctalia's lock screen
# listens to, so there is ONE lock code path. It also holds its own logind
# sleep inhibitor and locks before suspend ([lockscreen] lock_before_suspend,
# on by default), so there is no `lock` or `before-sleep` handler here: a
# second locker would only race it, and niri refuses whichever loses.
# swaylock-effects is still installed; to go back, restore the handlers from
# git history.

# Idle: at 5 min request a lock, at ~10 min blank the monitors.
timeout 301 'loginctl lock-session'
timeout 601 'niri msg action power-off-monitors'
